# Live smoke test (tools/live_smoke.sh, docs/ci.md "Live smoke tests"): spells and buffs.
# live-smoke: caster
# Played as the caster character (a GM cleric of any level on the same account; LIVE_SMOKE_CASTER). Memorize a buff,
# cast it on ourselves and click it off; memorize a short buff, cast it and let it wear off; memorize a nuke and cast
# it on a spawned NPC. Gem 8 is used and keeps the last spell. Stock PEQ's Qeynos Hills.
zone qeytoqrg
# Level 1 cleric spells, scribed if the book lacks them (otherwise the server says it cannot, harmlessly).
say #scribespell 202
say #scribespell 210
say #scribespell 14
# Start with no buffs (#nukebuffs, on ourselves: nothing is targeted after a login), so none blocks the ones cast here.
say #nukebuffs
wait 2
expect-no-buff 202
memorize 202 8
cast 8
expect-buff 202
click-off 202
expect-no-buff 202
# Yaulp lasts 4 ticks (about 24 s); the server's OP_Buff fade takes it off.
memorize 210 8
cast 8
expect-buff 210
fade 210 90
expect-no-buff 210
# A nuke on an NPC: the server lands it and reports its damage. #damage then kills the NPC (it has no loot).
say #spawn Smoke_Target 1 5 0 5000
wait 2
memorize 14 8
cast 8 Smoke_Target
kill Smoke_Target
